    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51446" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vultur</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volt-</span></b> ), ŭris, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in
				Apulia</i>, <i>near Venusia</i>, now <i>Monle Vulture</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 9, 185</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulturnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volt-</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Vultur</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventus,</span>”
				<i>a southeastby-one-third-south wind</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 47, 46, § 119</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 5, 16, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 5, 5,
				15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2,
			65</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 22, 11</span></i>; App. de Mundo, p. 63,
			14.</div>
